<crash-analysis>
The memory leak is caused by a bug in the `TY_(freeStack)` function in `/src/tidy-html5/src/lexer.c`. This function is responsible for freeing the memory allocated for a `Stack` structure, but it only frees the `firstNode` member of the stack and not the `stack` object itself.

To fix this bug, the `TY_(freeStack)` function should be modified to also free the `stack` object. The following line should be added to the function:

```c
TidyFree(stack->allocator, stack);
```

The corrected function should look like this:

```c
void TY_(freeStack)(Stack *stack)
{
TidyFree(stack->allocator, stack->firstNode);
TidyFree(stack->allocator, stack);
stack->top = -1;
stack->capacity = 0;
}
```
</crash-analysis>

